<title>ESTONIA: UHISPANK ITALIAN INVESTOR STAKE FALLS TO 16 PCT.</title>
<headline>UHISPANK ITALIAN INVESTOR STAKE FALLS TO 16 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stake of Italian investors in Uhispank has decreased from over 20 percent to 16 percent, the bank's vice-president said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Uhispank's Italian large investor Ernesto Preatoni has not sold his nine percent stake in Uhispank, vice-president Janek Maggi told Reuters.</p>
<p>Other Italian investors related to Preatoni's business interests have sold over seven percent of Uhispank shares and their stake has decreased to seven percent, he added.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
